CAT = "s63Remedies"; SEG = "REM"
Q = [
("Under the Uniform Securities Act, which action requires the Administrator to go to court?",
 "Obtaining an injunction", ["Issuing a cease and desist order", "Issuing a subpoena", "Denying a registration"],
 "The Administrator issues cease and desist orders and subpoenas and denies registrations directly, but must apply to a court for an injunction, a receiver or restitution."),
("Under the USA, the Administrator may conduct investigations:",
 "Within or outside the state", ["Only within the state", "Only with SEC approval", "Only after a court order"],
 "Section 407 lets the Administrator make public or private investigations within or outside the state when needed to find out whether anyone has violated or is about to violate the act."),
("A firm refuses to obey the Administrator's subpoena. The Administrator may:",
 "Ask a court to compel it", ["Jail the firm's officers", "Seize the firm's assets", "Fine the firm on the spot"],
 "On refusal to obey a subpoena, the Administrator may apply to a court, which can order compliance and punish failure to obey as contempt."),
("Under the USA, the Administrator may issue a cease and desist order:",
 "With or without a prior hearing", ["Only after a full hearing", "Only with a court's consent", "Only against unregistered firms"],
 "When a person is engaging or about to engage in a violation, the Administrator may order it to stop with or without a prior hearing, and the person may then request one."),
("After a summary order postponing or suspending a registration, a hearing must begin, if requested in writing, within:",
 "15 days of the request", ["10 days of the request", "30 days of the request", "60 days of the request"],
 "The Administrator must promptly notify the person of a summary order and the right to a hearing. On a written request, the matter is set for a hearing to begin within 15 days after the request is received."),
("The Administrator may deny an agent's registration if, within the past 10 years, she was convicted of:",
 "Any felony", ["Any misdemeanor", "Losing a civil lawsuit", "An unpaid parking ticket"],
 "Grounds include conviction within 10 years of any felony, or of a misdemeanor involving securities or the securities business. Other misdemeanors and civil suits are not automatic grounds."),
("The Administrator may NOT deny a registration solely because the applicant:",
 "Lacks experience", ["Is enjoined from selling securities", "Filed a misleading application", "Willfully broke the USA"],
 "The USA bars denial on the basis of lack of experience if the applicant is qualified by training, knowledge or both. Injunctions, misleading filings and willful violations are listed grounds."),
("The Administrator may cancel, rather than revoke, a registration when the registrant:",
 "Can no longer be located", ["Churned customer accounts", "Was convicted of fraud", "Made a false filing"],
 "Cancellation is used when a registrant has ceased to exist or do business, cannot be located, or has been found mentally incompetent. Misconduct leads to suspension or revocation instead."),
("An agent asks to withdraw her registration and no proceeding is pending. The withdrawal takes effect:",
 "30 days after it is filed", ["Immediately on filing", "At the end of the year", "60 days after it is filed"],
 "Withdrawal becomes effective 30 days after the Administrator receives the request, or sooner if the Administrator so orders, unless a revocation or suspension proceeding is pending."),
("After a withdrawal of registration takes effect, the Administrator may still start a revocation proceeding within:",
 "One year", ["30 days", "Two years", "Five years"],
 "The USA lets the Administrator institute a revocation or suspension proceeding within one year after a withdrawal became effective, so a registrant cannot escape discipline by quickly withdrawing."),
("A buyer sues an agent who sold her an unregistered, non-exempt stock. Under the USA she may recover the price paid plus:",
 "Interest, costs and legal fees", ["Triple damages", "Punitive damages only", "Nothing beyond the price"],
 "On tender of the security, the buyer recovers the consideration paid with interest at the legal rate, costs and reasonable attorneys' fees, less any income received on the security."),
("A seller sends a buyer a proper written offer to repurchase a security with interest. If the buyer does not accept within 30 days, she:",
 "Loses the right to sue", ["Can sue for triple damages", "Gets an extra year to decide", "May still sue anytime"],
 "A rescission offer that meets the USA's terms cuts off the buyer's civil suit if she fails to accept it within 30 days of receiving it."),
("An agent who materially aided an unlawful sale is liable to the buyer:",
 "Jointly with the seller", ["Only if she was paid", "Not at all", "Only to the Administrator"],
 "Every employee, agent or broker-dealer who materially aids the sale is jointly and severally liable with the seller, unless they did not know and could not reasonably have known of the facts."),
("Criminal penalties under the USA require that a violation be:",
 "Willful", ["Negligent", "Accidental", "Repeated three times"],
 "Criminal liability under Section 409 attaches to willful violations. Negligent conduct may still lead to administrative action or civil liability."),
("If the Administrator finds evidence of a criminal violation of the USA, the Administrator:",
 "Refers it to a prosecutor", ["Jails the violator", "Holds a criminal trial", "Sets the prison sentence"],
 "The Administrator may refer evidence to the attorney general or the proper district attorney, who decides whether to bring criminal proceedings. Only a court imposes criminal penalties."),
("A customer agreement says the customer waives her rights under the state securities act. That clause is:",
 "Void", ["Valid if in writing", "Valid for wealthy clients", "Valid if notarized"],
 "The USA voids any condition, stipulation or provision binding a person to waive compliance with the act or a rule or order under it."),
("Which customer loss is SIPC designed to cover?",
 "Assets missing at a failed firm", ["A drop in a stock's price", "Losses on commodity futures", "A bad recommendation"],
 "SIPC protects customers when a member broker-dealer fails and customer cash or securities are missing, up to its limits. It never covers market losses or poor advice."),
("Which of these held at a failed broker-dealer is NOT protected by SIPC?",
 "A fixed annuity contract", ["Common stock in the account", "Cash held to buy securities", "Treasury bonds in the account"],
 "SIPC covers securities and cash held for buying them. Fixed annuity contracts, commodity futures and currency positions are outside its protection."),
("The Administrator may issue a stop order against a securities registration if the offering:",
 "Pays unreasonable underwriter fees", ["Is from a new company", "Has a high price per share", "Comes from an out-of-state issuer"],
 "Grounds for a stop order include a misleading registration statement, illegality, fraud and unreasonable underwriting compensation or promoters' profits. A new issuer or high share price alone is not a ground."),
("Which is a ground for revoking a broker-dealer's registration?",
 "Failing to supervise its agents", ["A single losing year", "Charging disclosed commissions", "Being registered in other states"],
 "Failure to reasonably supervise agents or employees is a listed ground for denial, suspension or revocation when the order is in the public interest."),
("Under the USA, the Administrator may:",
 "Issue interpretive opinions", ["Guarantee registered securities", "Pass new statutes", "Award damages to investors"],
 "The Administrator may make rules and forms, issue orders and give interpretive opinions. Statutes come from the legislature, and damages are awarded by courts."),
("The Administrator may deny or suspend a broker-dealer's registration if the firm is:",
 "Insolvent", ["Newly formed", "Owned by a bank holding company", "Unprofitable last quarter"],
 "Insolvency, in the sense of liabilities exceeding assets or inability to meet obligations, is a listed ground. A new or briefly unprofitable firm is not insolvent."),
("An applicant is permanently enjoined by a court from engaging in the securities business. This is:",
 "Grounds to deny registration", ["Irrelevant after five years", "Only a FINRA matter", "Grounds only for a fine"],
 "Being subject to a court injunction against securities business activity is a listed ground for denial, suspension or revocation under Section 204."),
("A person aggrieved by a final order of the Administrator may seek review in:",
 "A state court", ["FINRA arbitration", "The SEC", "The state legislature"],
 "Section 411 lets a person aggrieved by a final order obtain review in the appropriate state court by filing a petition within 60 days after the order is entered."),
]
